{"assignees":[{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa","databaseId":12109493}],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"### Background\n\n#207 adds assignees and requested reviewers to the GitHub page, but the items aimed at me still blend into the list. As a cockpit for watching a busy repository, \"assigned to me\" and \"waiting for my review\" should stand out at a glance.\n\n### Proposal\n\n- GitHub list rows: when I am an assignee, render `@me` in yellow + bold; when my review is requested, render `→ me` in yellow; the row's leading icon also takes a dedicated \"for me\" color.\n- Detail header: highlight me in `Assignees:` / `Reviewers:` with the same color.\n- `m` toggles \"mine only\" (built like the `x` closed toggle, with `mine` shown in the header); the initial value comes from `github-mine-only \"on\"|\"off\"`.\n- Projects board: cards and table rows whose Assignees include me get the same highlight (filtering already exists via `assignee:@me`, so no new filter).\n\n### Scope\n\n- `src/github/panes/{issue_list,pr_list}.rs`, `panes/detail_view/view.rs` — rendering and the toggle\n- `src/projects/panes/board.rs` — card / row highlight\n- `src/core/config/` — `github-mine-only`\n- Demo: assign td72 on a PR / issue, then re-record the fixtures so the highlight appears in the GIFs\n- README / docs/README.ja.md / the guide (views-github, views-projects, config-reference)\n\n### Depends on\n\n- #207 (assignees / reviewers shown)\n- #208 (the signed-in login, resolved without an API call)\n\n### Notes\n\nRead-only as before.","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-11-04T04:21:25Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":209,"state":"OPEN","title":"Highlight the issues / PRs that are assigned to me or waiting for my review"}
